  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Recent public discussions have centered on potential candidates for the vice presidency in Indonesia, with Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, the Deputy Speaker of the House of Representatives, emerging as a frequently mentioned figure. Multiple groups, including the Indonesian Ulema Council (MUI) and various social organizations, have expressed public support for his candidacy, characterizing him as a trusted ally of President Prabowo Subianto. Political analysts have also highlighted his experience as a strategic coordinator in parliament as a factor that could bolster government unity. In response, Dasco has consistently maintained that the authority to designate a vice president resides solely with the head of state. Meanwhile, officials from the Gerindra party have urged the public and political observers to refrain from preemptive speculation until a formal announcement is made by the administration.",
